// Eyebite, sleep mode. Companion RONs eyebite_panicked.ron/
// eyebite_sickened.ron cover the other two submodes -- unlike
// minor_illusion_image.ron/minor_illusion_sound.ron (which share ONE
// compendium entry because only one mode is mechanically meaningful), each
// eyebite mode is a genuinely distinct effect the caster must pick between,
// so each gets its own compendium row (see compendium.ron's
// spells.necromancy.eyebite_* entries); there is no in-cast submode-selector
// UI, so "picking a mode" means casting the matching spell entry.
//
// Known simplification: the sheet lets the caster "turn that baleful eye
// upon a new victim within sight" every turn. No spell in this engine can
// retarget mid-concentration -- every Concentration effect is cast-and-lock,
// recast to pick a new target, same as `cause_fear`/`dread_whisper` and
// every other Concentration debuff already shipped.
BasicRanged(
    energy_cost: 100.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 8,
            buff: Some((
                kind: Asleep,
                dur_secs: 60,
                strength: Value(1.0),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            damage_kind: Necrotic,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 60.0,
    num_projectiles: Value(1),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Necromancy),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 6 spell -> min_level 36, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(36)),
    ),
)
